\\ D546_to302.gp -- ICARM curve #302 (rank 31) is a fibre of the member X_{2G} = surface(pt(2)) of D546_K3_family.gp.
\\ usage: gp -q --default parisizemax=1G D546_K3_family.gp D546_to302.gp
\\
\\ Source: https://elliptic-rank.icarm.cloud, curve #302 (snapshot of database.json, 2026-09-23).  Its commentary
\\ (edit by wgxli) gives #302 as the specialisation at T = 164518/924945 of the normal form
\\       y^2 - (L x + B) y = x (x + D)(x + E),   B = p q (L + p + q) - p E - q D,
\\ with the [L, p, q, D, E] of NF302_PUB below (no sections are published).
\\
\\ The change of coordinates.  A form f of weight k (k = 1: L, p, q;  k = 2: D, E, x;  k = 3: y) goes to
\\       f  ->  s^k (5T + 4)^(2k) f((19T + 8)/(5T + 4)),      s = -1/(2^3 3^13 29).
\\ This is a Moebius change of T with a scaling, so it is an isomorphism of elliptic surfaces over Q.
\\
\\ What this file checks:
\\   (1) it maps [L, p, q, D, E] of surface(pt(2)) exactly to the published #302 model;
\\   (2) it maps the 17 sections to sections of the #302 model with the Gram matrix of the family (det 1092, no roots,
\\       no even overlattice).  So the 17 sections generate the Mordell-Weil group of the #302 model over Q(T);
\\   (3) the fibre at T = 164518/924945 has the minimal model of #302;
\\   (4) the 31 published points lie on #302 and are independent (their height matrix has full rank).

w(f, k) = (-1/(2^3*3^13*29))^k * (5*'T + 4)^(2*k) * subst(f, 'T, (19*'T + 8)/(5*'T + 4));
{NF302_PUB = [446667*'T^2 + 471466*'T + 239031, 318552*'T^2 + 368554*'T - 72570,
  733413*'T^2 - 45082*'T - 14960, 5*(7174492962*'T^4 - 7114589515*'T^3 - 22069002960*'T^2 + 3909144679*'T - 205134150),
  882769396002*'T^4 + 811447034567*'T^3 - 1174040743*'T^2 - 32493137198*'T - 2386325360];}   \\ [L, p, q, D, E]
T302 = 164518/924945;
{E302 = ellinit([1, 1, 1,
  -1284727764113567728281797636015784768866707681415849262157224232063,
  560368321454261339256859338901915312332769858684945406858043869199456710681989058863306170127006181]);}   \\ ICARM #302
